<div class="accordion_content" id="{{ controls_id }}" markdown='1' hidden>

The `/reference/workbook/` location stores example datasets and reference results prepared for workbook tutorials. 
These files are shared, centrally maintained, and available in **read-only** mode so that all users can work from the same inputs without modifying them.

For most tutorials, it is better to read data directly from `/reference/workbook/` than to copy it into your own workspace:
- it avoids unnecessary duplication in `/90daydata/shared/$USER/`
- it reduces storage use in temporary practice space
- it keeps the tutorial inputs consistent across users and sessions

Create a local copy only when a tutorial explicitly requires one, for example when files must be edited, renamed, or rewritten in place.

